{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127796-hunter-second-edition-inspirations","id":1127796,"title":"Hunter Second Edition Inspirations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-11T15:15:52-07:00","id":1127796,"title":"Hunter Second Edition Inspirations","content":"We are having a blast working on the game, so I thought I'd pop in and kick off a fun conversation. Since Hunter first came out, there have been a ton of great books, movies, and TV shows that tap into different aspects. In this thread, list some of your faves! For example, the human faction in The Originals with their collection of dark objects are pretty cool. Quite a few Black Mirror episodes highlight technological advances while GRIMM and Supernatural are easy choices. That's just on the popular side of the equation! So, what kinds of things would you recommend to players devoting themselves to the Vigil for the first time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1870-mlvalentine","name":"mlvalentine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1870_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T15:28:08-07:00","id":1127799,"title":"","content":"The book London Falling is in my opinion the best story about regular mortals becoming hunters and finding their way around an unfamiliar supernatural landscape I've seen, recommended for Tier 1 play.<br /> <br /> Paravigilum from <a href=\"http://www.talesfromthevault.com/thunderstruck/\" target=\"_blank\">Thunderstruck</a> feels closer to a Hunter Conspiracy than anything else in the WoD, despite being run by supernaturals. And informs a fair bit about how I play Tier 3 groups. They may mostly be ordinary men with guns and training, but due to their sheer size, resources, and the ability to break out Endowments when needed even the most powerful supernaturals in the setting won't dare take them on head to head. (Also Bella Brouchard is perhaps the coolest charachter in all of Urban Fantasy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T15:50:07-07:00","id":1127805,"title":"","content":"Probably because the movie hype made me read the book again, but I'd suggest Stephen King's It.<br /> <br /> Then of course there's the Hellboy Universe, with all kinds of monster hunters from the ages, ranging from good devils to military organisations of all sorts, Victorian agents of the crown and Pulp crime fighters that stumble frequently on the supernatural world. All made more awesome from weird monsters, relics and mysteries. It's a <i>huge </i>source of inspirations for Hunter.<br /> <br /> I think I can come up with some more later","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:02:06-07:00","id":1127810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127796-hunter-second-edition-inspirations?p=1127805#post1127805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then of course there's the Hellboy Universe, with all kinds of monster hunters from the ages, ranging from good devils to military organisations of all sorts, Victorian agents of the crown and Pulp crime fighters that stumble frequently on the supernatural world. All made more awesome from weird monsters, relics and mysteries. It's a <i>huge </i>source of inspirations for Hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Some of all of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:04:50-07:00","id":1127812,"title":"","content":"True Detective (the first season; let's all pretend there is no second one) is about as perfect as I could ask for. Two cops get drawn into a supernatural mystery, and their hunt for the truth and the person/monster/??? at the heart of it takes an immense cost on their bodies, minds, and personal lives. That's the core of the Vigil for me; the CofD is a world where everyone keeps their heads down, and hunters are the rare few idiots who refuse to do that even if it destroys them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:15:36-07:00","id":1127814,"title":"","content":"Jessica Jones might be a superhero herself, but honestly, her struggle against Kilgrave feels a lot like a normal person trying to deal with a mind-controller. It helps that her powers are pretty low-key in the show. She's super-strong, and Luke Cage is nigh-invulnerable, but both offer little protection from Kilgrave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 08-11-2017, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:42:47-07:00","id":1127825,"title":"","content":"Seconding True Detective and Hellboy. Also, obvious pick is obvious, but Stranger Things. <br /> <br /> Even though they were around for Hunter 1e, I'd also suggest the Sigma Force Novels by James Rollins. They focus more on science, but there are levels of the occult and supernatural layered in there too. It's a good idea of what would happe if Taskforce VALKERIE teamed up with Null Mysteriis.<br /> <br /> Actually, pretty much everything by James Rollins would work well for Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T16:58:12-07:00","id":1127832,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Inspirations</b><br /> <br /> When my mind turns to characters that hunt the supernatural, my list of influences are really long and eclectic, but the following are some of the sources that rise to the surface time and time again and are mostly Hunter -specific.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friday_the_13th:_The_Series\" target=\"_blank\">Friday the 13th -The Series</a>: This was an syndicated series that revolved around a pair of relatively normal people who inherited a shop full of cursed relics. I've been fascinated by the trope ever since.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vampire$\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire$</a>: A novel by John Steakley - the titular company is a group of Vampire Hunters who charge a fee for their services. The hunters maintained a very &quot;eat drink, and be merry&quot; lifestyle. That sort of joyously fatalistic attitude really resonated with how I think a person would cope with a intensely dangerous (and potentially damning) lifestyle.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/The_Hunters_Hunted\" target=\"_blank\">The Hunter's Hunted</a>: The first World of Darkness book that dealt specifically with Vampire Hunters. The artwork exceptional, and while very much a product of early White Wolf, it holds up well. The book also offers the first glimpse of what would eventually evolve in the Werewolves and Mages of the Classic WoD. The quote on the first page still sums up what I think being a Hunter is all about -<br /> <br /> <b><i>Too often humans scurry in fear of the dark. Too often they curry favor with the lords of evil. Too often they are weak, petty, vain or foolish. But not all, and not always. The battle is joined.</i></b><br /> <br /> I also found good material from a few non White Wolf/ Onyx Path rpgs, Such as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beyond_the_Supernatural\" target=\"_blank\">Beyond the Supernatural</a>, and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Flesh_Must_Be_Eaten\" target=\"_blank\">All Flesh Must be Eaten</a>.<br /> <br /> For more recent material, I have been greatly impressed by the series <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gravity_Falls\" target=\"_blank\">Gravity Falls</a>, which depicts awesome ways to bring a amazing degree of weirdness to a game without ever going above a PG 13 rating. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:01:50-07:00","id":1127834,"title":"","content":"Omg, yes Gravity Falls!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:36:16-07:00","id":1127845,"title":"","content":"The Laundry books are a decent look at a Conspiracy, especially one that has to deal with other Conspiracies. The mojo is a bit more understood and employed, but it shows the toys/Endowments can be broken out when needed (and how risky even using them can be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:45:36-07:00","id":1127854,"title":"","content":"<i>Hannibal </i>is great example of a Slasher and a Hunter having a really complicated relationship, and what happens when you look too hard into the light of Vigil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-12-2017, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T17:46:50-07:00","id":1127855,"title":"","content":"XCom: Enemy Unknown and it's sequel really capture the idea of a third tier Hunter Chronicle from the perspective of the head of a Conspiracy. You start out completely out numbered by an unknowable but distinctively more powerful force of monsters (and human collaborators) but through strategy, research and the occasional hard choice to sacrifice a solider or even a nation you can gain the upper hand. Both games offer more closure than you're likely to see in any CoD but it's a place to start.<br /> <br /> Darkest Dungeon: Same general idea as XCom. You're a human meat grinder of a boss trying to deal with an otherworldly portal letting untold horrors into the world. Tapping adventurers to breaking points of mind and body until they are of no more use.<br /> <br /> Ghostbusters: All versions of this franchise are a great (albeit less than serious) looks at ordinary folks getting way over their heads and delving head first into the supernatural. Maybe too serious for the corebook but certainly something to consider at your own table.<br /> <br /> Daredevil: Not so much the plot or characters (which are both great make no mistake) but the fight choreography nails the sense of desperate brutality that you want in your hunter games.<br /> <br /> and an honourable mention<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B074QNS9S3\" target=\"_blank\">#iHunt</a> by former Onyx Path dev David Hill. I haven't gotten to read it yet, since it just came out today but from his description on twitter makes direct mention of a lot of the themes in Hunter that I love so I imagine it'll be a relevant read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:02:16-07:00","id":1127861,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Enemy Unknown</b><br /> <br /> Total Agreement! In my various homebrew projects I have a partial XCom conversion - many of the ideas I used for that wandered into my regular games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:07:18-07:00","id":1127865,"title":"","content":"I started doing Horror stats for the XCom aliens a while ago but never finished. I really should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9065-darkblade","name":"Darkblade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:29:53-07:00","id":1127872,"title":"","content":"Werewolf the Forsaken, second edition. With the shift in focus to 'The Wolf Must Hunt,' it's hard not to see the vigil as a mortal vestige of Father Wolf and the Uratha. The fiction, sans werewolf abilities, is about a cell of hunters whose lives have been overturned at a great threat they can't exactly explain to the authorities. They devote years and lives to putting an end to the threat, which just gets bigger and more pervasive while they try and find an angle to come at it that will end it for all. And in the end they do so, but not without loss, sacrifice, and deals that perhaps should not have been made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T18:42:08-07:00","id":1127880,"title":"","content":"The <i>Predator</i> movies<br /> <br /> To varying degrees they do capture the idea of a group of armed, well-trained individuals that have to deal with something utterly inhuman, with superior technology and abilities, and how woefully unprepared they are. And how even for a group of soldier meatheads, the unknown monster(s) in the jungles can be utterly terrifying.<br /> <br /> The third movie, <i>Predators</i>, even has an example of a hunter (Lawrence Fishburne's character) that's become so utterly paranoid and survivalist that he's willing to kill off the first human contact that he's seen in years, just to take his stuff.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, <i>Aliens</i>. Just because you have the biggest and most amount of guns doesn't mean you are any more prepared to deal with the creatures in the night.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, you could characterize the Predator aliens as being Slashers if you so wish: unstoppable killing machines that actually are inhuman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 08-11-2017, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T19:02:26-07:00","id":1127883,"title":"","content":"I Death Note.<br /> <br /> Ex-Hunter turns into a Slasher and goes off the deep end when he gets a hold of Supernatural power. Probably what it looks like when one of the Lucifuge goes AWOL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 08-12-2017, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T22:50:18-07:00","id":1127931,"title":"","content":"This is an award winning short that to me depicts the Malleus Maleficarum in all it's awesome glory:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o5bsDhYbETY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o5bsDhYbETY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o5bsDhYbETY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=o5bsDhYbETY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T23:06:42-07:00","id":1127936,"title":"","content":"The Keepers. It deals with human evils that remind us however dark a world we imagine for our games it will never be as dark as the world we're actually living in. <br /> <br /> On a lighter note both Ash vs The Evil Dead and John Dies At The End give us a take on the Vigil as gruesome farce.<br /> <br /> While I don't personally care for it as a series, the Conjuring franchise has in it a solid Hunter framework.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T23:29:10-07:00","id":1127945,"title":"","content":"How about <i>Stranger Things</i>? While a couple characters, especially the older siblings in high school, hunted the monster itself (whereas the middle schoolers found themselves in a <i>Deviant</i> campaign side-by-side with a <i>Hunter</i> one), the sheriff really started spiraling down the Hunter life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T05:29:54-07:00","id":1128015,"title":"","content":"Penny Dreadful, perhaps? Part of the main cast are supernaturals, but a good part of the show arcs are all about dealing with monsters as hunters, after all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T15:14:29-07:00","id":1128214,"title":"","content":"Dracula is in many ways more a Hunter novel than a Vampire one.<br /> <br /> The Inspector McLean novels of James Oswald are about a Glasgow police inspector trying not to believe he's taken up the Vigil, and how his life intersects with people who know better.<br /> <br /> The Exorcism of Emily Rose is about a lawyer's first brush with the maybe-supernatural, and the question of whether she'll keep looking at the dark.<br /> <br /> Weirdly perhaps, Pretty Little Liars. They're not facing anything supernatural - you could characterise some of their enemies as Genius slashers, but others are just mundane criminals. But they're a small group targeted by forces only they can see, and which they have to keep secret for the safety of the people around them. It shows both resourcefulness and mistakes as they investigate, is full of secrets and sins on all sides, has a shady mental hospital at the centre of everything, and shows the slow disintegration of the heroines' lives and how hard it is for them to maintain relationships with people outside their &quot;cell.&quot; It also has a more strictly supernatural spinoff, but that didn't last long (and I haven't seen it).<br /> <br /> The Bletchley Circle is a great model for a hunter cell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T10:31:52-07:00","id":1130342,"title":"","content":"Can I propose <b>Secret World</b> MMO? It's background is based on 3 ancient Conspiracies fighting united against monsters ( of Darkness ) and each other over arcane secrets all over the world ( and time! ). Power level of gameplay maybe a bit over even <b>HtV</b> Tier 3 games, but the feel of plot is exactly what I think about running Conspiracies in <b>Hunter</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Especially as main plot of game is about fighting mystical alien disease, like in coming <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book\">Contagion Chronicle book</a> for <b>CoD</b> universe. Did I added that <b>Secret World</b> it's now totally free video game and TV series is in the works? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W9gQ2OeZ7V4\" data-code=\"W9gQ2OeZ7V4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/W9gQ2OeZ7V4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-17-2017, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T12:29:07-07:00","id":1130402,"title":"","content":"If other tabletop games are allowed, then I can't praise the new standalone <b>Delta Green</b> enough. It's about a semi-sanctioned conspiracy within the American federal government (primarily law enforcement, intelligence, and military, though every branch can technically be in on it) fighting the forces of the Cthulhu Mythos, but it leans incredibly hard into the grit of keeping up the Vigil. Not only is focused on the high lethality and intense cost to mental health that most Cthulhu games features, it also mechanically codifies your important interpersonal relationships and has optional rules for trying to maintain your cover job as well; agents are almost certainly locked into a spiral of burning bridges with the people they care about as they're forced to lie about what they've seen and done. It's intense as hell, and is exactly what I want out of my Hunter games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:07:49-07:00","id":1130564,"title":"","content":"It may sound weird, but the noir feel to movies like and shows like Riverdale make me think of Hunters and the shadowy side of humanity. more overtly supernatural themes would be Denzel Washington's Fallen and the tv show Supernatural and the old tv show Carnivale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:28:36-07:00","id":1130577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127796-hunter-second-edition-inspirations?p=1130564#post1130564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may sound weird, but the noir feel to movies like and shows like Riverdale make me think of Hunters and the shadowy side of humanity. more overtly supernatural themes would be Denzel Washington's Fallen and the tv show Supernatural and the old tv show Carnivale.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a similar note, Archie's Wierd Mysteries is probably a good place to look for teens dealing with supernatural shit in a way that isn't overly graphic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"h