src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Childrens-Vampire-Hunting-Brigade-Vol/dp/0983686475\" target=\"_blank\"> Amazon.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Childrens-Vampire-Hunting-Brigade-Vol/dp/0983686475\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Childrens-Vampire-Hunting-Brigade-Vol/dp/0983686475 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T08:01:11-07:00","id":1130820,"title":"","content":"Murdock Mysteries. Not exactly supernatural, but sometimes its gets close, like Dr. Sorbay. <br /> <br /> Murdoch, Dr. Ogdin, Constable Crabtree, Brackenreid would make an excellent hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T10:46:30-07:00","id":1130888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1127796-hunter-second-edition-inspirations?p=1130820#post1130820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Murdock Mysteries. Not exactly supernatural, but sometimes its gets close, like Dr. Sorbay.<br /> <br /> Murdoch, Dr. Ogdin, Constable Crabtree, Brackenreid would make an excellent hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that show!! Ogdin would be a great Null Mysterriis. Crabtree and Brackenreid I see as very Union. Murdoch I could see as some mix of Union, Null Mysteriis, Malleus Maleficarum mix<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T08:35:10-08:00","id":1191945,"title":"","content":"Despite the protagonist being a wizard and bumping shoulders with the supernaturally powerful, Dresden Files is a good resource as many times it shows ordinary humans fighting monsters. From Special Investigations to The Knights of The Cross to Marcone's crime syndicate, it can really display the power mortals have when they band together. The Ranger's Apprentice books may also be good, thre may not be so much in the way of monster hunting but it shows ordinary people using cunning, planning and ingenuity to solve problems way above them. Many of the older Anthology shows reminiscent of the midnight society, goosebumps despite its leaning to a younger audience is still about mortals fighting the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T16:37:03-08:00","id":1192086,"title":"","content":"So it may be too late, but I had a thought on my way home. You could get a lot of ideas for Network Zero/Null Mysteriis tactics and tricks out of National Geographic Live. These are presentations given Nat Geo authors, scientists, and photographers about their stories and discoveries around the world and the lengths they go to get them. If you can see a show in your city, they are seriously worth it, but if not, you can find lots of the lecture series on YouTube.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T19:38:35-08:00","id":1192117,"title":"","content":"<i>Bloodborne </i>will always be my point of reference for Hunter the Vigil. Especially in the Dark Eras homebrew I'm running which takes great inspiration from the game. Observing the way the Factions intermingled and eventually fell as a lone Hunter is an infested city is a beautiful example of environmental storytelling. The threats are severe and dangerous and you have to always be prepared when you step into a fight or it means your death and a return to the Dream.<br /> <br /> Dating this post (3/5/18) but at the moment Bloodborne is free to PS Plus subscribers so if you haven't played it, I recommend it highly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10827-baronzobops","name":"baronzobops","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10827_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T13:04:26-08:00","id":1192359,"title":"","content":"Another suggestion for Network Zero would be <i>Tales by Light</i>. It is a photography documentary that does both nature and cultural pieces. Depending on which monsters you are hunting, there could be some neat tricks for capturing animals/people on camera that the Network could use. You can find it on Netflix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-06-2018, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T07:06:21-07:00","id":1194236,"title":"","content":"<i>Kong: Skull Island</i>. Ignore the film's flaws and some of its over-the-top silliness, and you have a fairly wide array of Hunters portrayed very well:<br /> <br /> Lt. Colonel Preston Packard (Samuel L. Jackson's character): The Hunter who quite quickly jumps off the slippery slope and decides that if I don't like it, it dies. Made more complex by his interactions with his soldiers: on one hand, he could easily be seen as A Father To His Men, but there's just enough hints of callousness there that he could just be playing that role to win their loyalty, and doesn't give a damn about their lives as long as he completes his objective.<br /> <br /> William Randa (John Goodman's character): The well-intentioned extremist, who knows monsters are real, knows no one's listening to him, knows that they'll cause untold devastation if we continue to ignore them, and needs proof to round up enough firepower to start putting them down. He may be starting a change of heart, realizing that there are &quot;good&quot; monsters, or he may still believe that humanity can only be safe once they're all dead.<br /> <br /> Houston Brooks (Corey Hawkins character): The scholar, the information seeker. He wants to know what's out there, why it's out there, and how it fits into the world. He's open-minded and ready to change his beliefs as new evidence comes in.<br /> <br /> James Conrad (Tom Hiddleston's character): The expert, the man with the mad skills. He happens to learn that his skills are just as applicable in this world of monsters. Could easily have gone the other way.<br /> <br /> Mason Weaver (Brie Larson's character): The truth-seeker, the one who wants to yank the veil of secrecy away. Notably changes her mind at the end of the film, deciding that the world is better off not knowing about Kong and Skull Island. Relates to Hunters who both want to blow all the various conspiracies of the supernatural wide open and the ones who quietly collect their information, knowing the world is not ready to know what they know, but one day they might be. And in the meantime, knowledge is power.<br /> <br /> Hank Marlow (John C. Reilly's character): The survivor, the one who's been neck-deep in this crap for the longest, the one who knows how this world works, and the one you'd damn well better listen to if you want to survive past today. A more comedic take on this type character than usual, but pretty much everything bad that happens after his introduction to the film is a direct result of his advice being flagrantly ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}